# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext" "A sigil's marker reads as the dialect's keyword"

# TiddlyWiki reads `<<~ set …>>` as a call on a variable spelled `~`, and the base names that `~`
# as the called name. The dialect names it BESIDE that reading as the sigil's MARKER — the glyph
# every sigil opens with, closers included (`<<~/ahu>>`) — and it reads as the dialect's keyword.
# The rule fires only where the base already reads a call name, so a `~` anywhere else keeps its
# own reading, and the word "macro" in a sentence stays prose.

<<~ set hud="aim">>
# ^ punctuation.definition.sigil.marker.memetic-wikitext
# ^ keyword.control.sigil.marker.memetic-wikitext
# ^ entity.name.function.procedure.tiddlywiki5

<<~/ahu>>
# ^ keyword.control.sigil.marker.memetic-wikitext
#  ^ punctuation.definition.sigil.close.memetic-wikitext

# CONTROLS: a tilde outside a call, a call on any other name, and prose.
About ~5 macro calls stand in this sentence, and a macro reads as a word.
#     ^ - keyword.control.sigil.marker.memetic-wikitext
#        ^^^^^ - keyword.control.sigil.marker.memetic-wikitext
#        ^^^^^ - keyword.control.sigil.memetic-wikitext

<<greet "a~b">>
#         ^ - keyword.control.sigil.marker.memetic-wikitext

<!-- <<~ set>> -->
#      ^ - keyword.control.sigil.marker.memetic-wikitext

```
<<~ set>>
# ^ - keyword.control.sigil.marker.memetic-wikitext
```

$$$text/plain
<<~ set>>
# ^ - keyword.control.sigil.marker.memetic-wikitext
$$$
